#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rgos-sticks: RG OS input hub = gpio-keys buttons + ADC analog sticks -> ONE virtual gamepad.

Why: the RG34XX-SP sticks are read by the ROCKNIX-only `rocknix-singleadc-joypad` driver (a 4:1 analog mux driven by
two GPIOs in front of one GPADC channel). That driver does not bind on our kernel, so tools/dtb_gpiokeys.py moves the
buttons to the stock gpio-keys driver and disables the joypad node, which dropped the sticks. This daemon is the
userspace replacement for the sticks:

  * reads the wiring from the (disabled but still present) /proc/device-tree/rocknix-singleadc-joypad node:
    amux-a/b-gpios (mux select lines), amux-channel-mapping, io-channels (GPADC channel), invert-abs* flags;
  * drives the mux through the GPIO character device and reads the GPADC through IIO sysfs;
  * grabs the raw "gpio-keys-joypad" device and re-publishes its buttons together with the 4 stick axes as one
    uinput device, "RG OS Gamepad" (same key codes => same SDL/RetroArch button numbers as before; axes are
    ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_RX, ABS_RY => SDL axes 0..3).

If the sticks cannot be read (no GPADC, no GPIO chip...) the buttons are still forwarded and the axes stay at 0.
If the hub cannot start at all (no /dev/uinput) the raw gpio-keys device is left alone, exactly like before.

Other devices (TrimUI Smart Pro, written without hardware): the hub is device-agnostic.
  * "sources": which input devices to merge: ["gpio-keys-joypad"] (default when the ROCKNIX joypad node exists in the
    device tree = RG34XX-SP) or "auto" (every event device that has gamepad buttons or X/Y axes; power/volume/lid/touch
    devices are skipped). A list of name substrings picks devices by hand.
  * every source key is translated to a canonical code (the codes retroarch.cfg and gamecontrollerdb.txt are written for):
    known BTN_* codes pass through, ABS_HAT0X/Y become the D-pad, anything else comes from the table the menu's
    Settings > Map buttons wizard saved in /var/lib/rgos/button-map.json (or "keymap" {"<code>": "<canonical code>"} in input.json).
  * sticks: "mode" in the "sticks" object = "adc-mux" (RG34XX-SP default: the mux/GPADC reader above), "evdev" (default
    elsewhere: the sources' own ABS_X/Y/RX/RY are scaled to +-32767; "axis_map" {"<abs code>": 0..3}, "invert" per axis)
    or "none" (buttons only).
  /etc/rgos/input-<device>.json (device = /etc/rgos-device) is merged over input.json.

usage: rgos-sticks             run the hub (systemd service rgos-sticks)
       rgos-sticks probe       live raw/normalised stick values on the terminal (stop the service first)
       rgos-sticks reset-cal   forget the learned stick calibration (/var/lib/rgos/sticks.json)
       rgos-sticks reset-map   forget the axis mapping chosen by the menu's stick wizard (back to the DTB's)
       rgos-sticks reset-buttons   forget the button mapping saved by the menu's Map buttons wizard

Config: optional "sticks" object in /etc/rgos/input.json, all keys optional:
  "enabled": true, "poll_ms": 10, "settle_us": 400, "deadzone": 0.10,
  "mux_map": [0,2,1,3]      mux select -> axis index (0=X 1=Y 2=RX 3=RY); default = what the stick wizard saved in
                            /var/lib/rgos/stick-map.json, else amux-channel-mapping from the DTB
  "invert":  [true,true,true,true]   per axis X,Y,RX,RY; default = wizard, else invert-absx/y/rx/ry from the DTB
  "gpio_chip": "/dev/gpiochipN", "iio_dir": "/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceN"   override auto-detection
"""
